  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be a differentiable function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.<br />Consider the following two statements:</p><p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>for&#160;all</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>(B)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>for&#160;all</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Then,</p>"
  },
